+# Veterinarian Directory Filtering Narrows NG-9 and Stays a URL Contract
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian. The row was derived from observed absence, and its wording left filtering the veterinarian directory unaddressed at best and excluded at worst. The owner requested a filter by specialty on both veterinarian surfaces, so the boundary needed an explicit decision.
+
+The owner decided the boundary in the 2026-10-31 request, quoted here:
+
+> Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in.
+
+> The filter is a URL contract only. Neither surface gains a form, dropdown, or other page control in this request; pagination links carry the parameter so filtered pages stay navigable. A visible control may come as a follow-up request.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 as written.** Rejected by the owner: it would decline the requested filter.
+2. **Retire NG-9.** Not chosen: the owner keeps free-text veterinarian search out of scope, and the request does not touch pet or visit search.
+3. **Narrow NG-9 and record the absent control as NG-10** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 remains in force for searching pets, visits, and veterinarians, free-text veterinarian search included. Filtering the veterinarian directory by an attribute it already shows is outside the non-goal.
+
+NG-10 declines a form, dropdown, or other page control for the specialty filter on either surface. The owner leaves a follow-up request open, so NG-10 holds until such a request carries an owner decision.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The specialty filter is reachable only by URL. A reader on the directory page has no visible way to apply it.
+- Attributes beyond specialty are not opened by this decision. Each still needs its own request.
+- Pet and visit search stay declined. Their provenance stays part of the open consultation.
+- The owner stated no reason for either decision, so this record gives none beyond the quotes.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9, NG-10
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and the new row.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the requirement the narrowing admits.
